            "english_quote": "that assigns the forms to fears in the cheek and to desire",
            "issue": "The draft attempts to represent every printed word, but it does not establish a defensible contextual meaning for παρίᾳ. Identifying that printed form provisionally with a noun meaning “cheek” and then construing it as a locative within τοῖς ... φόβοις does not adequately support the assertion that the fears are “in the cheek.” The proposed facial manifestation of fear is an additional explanatory hypothesis, not an established meaning of this construction. The notes honestly disclose the unresolved problem, but disclosure cannot validate unsupported main-text wording. This is a remaining lexical and constructional meaning problem, not an unverified transcription or merely a choice between demonstrated alternatives.",
